  "gotchas": [
    "Auth (OAuth2 client credentials): POST grant_type=client_credentials, client_id and client_secret as application/x-www-form-urlencoded to https://idp.flutterwave.com/realms/flutterwave/protocol/openid-connect/token (same token URL for sandbox and production), then send `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`. Docs (Authentication): \"Each token is valid for **10 minutes**\"; \"We recommend refreshing the token at least one minute before it expires.\" Cache the token. FLUTTERWAVE_CLIENT_CREDENTIALS = base64(client_id:client_secret) is an afrotools convention, decoded locally; Flutterwave never receives it. Sandbox base URL: https://developersandbox-api.flutterwave.com (\"We archive your test data after 30 days.\")",
    "Headers: X-Trace-Id is optional on this PUT (the headers guide lists it under 'Optional API Headers'; \"It must be a string using only alphanumeric ASCII characters.\", 12-255 characters). The API reference documents no X-Idempotency-Key for this endpoint.",
    "authorization is an object discriminated on type: {type:'pin', pin:{nonce, encrypted_pin}}, {type:'otp', otp:{code}}, {type:'avs', avs:{address:{…}}}, or {type:'external_3ds', external_3ds:{…all eight fields required}}.",
    "PIN then OTP: \"You’ll first need to update the charge with the encrypted card PIN.\" \"Followed by updating the charge request with the OTP.\" Read data.next_action after every update.",
    "AVS: Docs (Card Payments): \"If the charge response contains `data.next_action.requires_additional_fields`, it means that you are charging an AVS card.\" next_action.requires_additional_fields.fields lists dotted body paths (e.g. authorization.avs.address.postal_code).",
    "Card encryption: Docs (Encryption): \"When making a card charge request, you **must encrypt** the card information before sending the request.\" \"Retrieve your encryption key from the **API settings** section in your Flutterwave dashboard.\" The documented Node sample encrypts each field with AES-GCM (\"name: \"AES-GCM\"\"): key = the base64-decoded encryption key, IV = the UTF-8 bytes of the nonce (\"Nonce must be exactly 12 characters long\"), output = base64 of the ciphertext. Send the same nonce in the request (card.nonce / pin.nonce). Bad encryption: \"we'll return a `422` error with a failed encryption error message.\" The page's sample error has code 11100, the error table lists 1137400 (a 400): branch on error.type CLIENT_ENCRYPTION_ERROR. FLUTTERWAVE_ENCRYPTION_KEY is an afrotools env-var name; the docs name none. Official backend SDKs encrypt for you.",
    "The API reference lists 200/400/401/403 for this PUT (no 409): a finalised charge fails with 1111400 CHARGE_FINALIZED.",
    "The card guide's PIN, OTP and AVS update requests all send X-Idempotency-Key although the API reference doesn't list it here: sending one is harmless; use a new key per update (PIN and OTP are two operations).",
    "Errors: {\"status\":\"failed\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\",\"validation_errors\"}}; error.code is a string and 400s carry validation_errors[{field_name,message}]. Besides the generic codes (10400 REQUEST_NOT_VALID, 10401, 10403 FORBIDDEN, 10404 RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND, 10409 RESOURCE_CONFLICT, 10422 UNPROCESSABLE, 10500) the error table documents these for this endpoint: 1110404 CHARGE_NOT_FOUND, 1111400 CHARGE_FINALIZED (already succeeded or failed), 1112400 CHARGE_UPDATE_NOT_ALLOWED, 1134422 CARD_EXPIRED, 1113500 CHARGE_UPDATE_FAILED, 1121400 INVALID_AUTHORIZATION (wrong PIN or OTP), 1137400 CLIENT_ENCRYPTION_ERROR. Branch on error.type / error.code, not on the HTTP status alone. Docs (Errors): \"The current limit is 500 API requests per minute.\" A 429 can come back as a non-JSON page (\"HTML error pages such as `Cloudflare 1015 responses`\"): parse error bodies defensively and back off exponentially with jitter."
  ],
